      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The Mpemba effect is the phenomenon where hotter water can sometimes freeze
    faster than colder water. This study found that the effect can be reproduced
    by increasing the number of nucleation sites in the warmer sample''s container.
    Surprisingly, hot water could still freeze faster even when it required over
    50% more energy to cool. However, results vary greatly depending on the liquid''s
    exact chemistry, and this should not be taken as a universally applicable effect. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
