  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Abstract\r\nIn this report, we studied three Ornithorhynchus anatinus
    specimens under visible and ultraviolet light(UV). The animal\u2019s pelts appeared
    uniformly brown under visible light and green or cyan under UV light due to fluorescent
    wavelengths. Our observations are the first report of biofluorescence in monotreme
    mammals. \n\r\nFurther research is required to determine the true nature of this
    trait. However, three theories stand: first, it may help them blend into the
    low-light environment of a moonlit river; second, it might reduce contrast against
    UV-sensitive predators; and third, it could simply be an ancient vestigial trait."
